Circle \(C\) passes through \(A(6,11)\) and is centred at \(G(0,3)\).
(a)Find the equation of \(C\).
(b)A moving point \(P\) satisfies \(AP=GP\), with locus \(\Gamma\).
(i)Find \(\Gamma\);
(ii)describe its relation to \(AG\);
(iii)if \(\Gamma\) cuts \(C\) at \(Q,R\), find the perimeter of \(AQGR\).

Points \(A,B\) are \((-10,0),(30,0)\). Circle \(C\) passes through them, and the y-coordinate of its centre \(G\) is \(-15\).
(a)Find \(C\).
(b)Line \(L\) passes through \(B,G\), and line \(\ell\) is parallel to \(L\). A moving point \(P\) is equidistant from \(L,\ell\), with locus \(\Gamma\) passing through \(A\).
(i)Describe the relation between \(\Gamma\) and \(L\);
(ii)find \(\Gamma\);
(iii)if \(\Gamma\) cuts \(C\) again at \(H\), someone claims \(\angle GAH<70^\circ\). Do you agree?
